<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE nrol-136 ascent</name><description>FLOWN / RETIMED 2026-11-22: T0 is the actual liftoff 2026-11-22T12:23:56Z (Sun 22 Nov 4:23:56 a.m. PST). LL2 id 951a341f-236b-42fe-a667-4ab2fcf36eac is Launch Successful, net to the second, last_updated 2026-11-22T14:41:24Z. SpaceX post-flight page: liftoff Sunday 22 Nov at 4:23 a.m. PT, 14th flight, landing LZ-4 (https://www.spacex.com/launches/nrol136). SpaceX liftoff and LZ-4 landing post https://x.com/SpaceX/status/2124479235779637392. Spaceflight Now https://x.com/SpaceflightNow/status/2124479451878830301 says 4:23 a.m. PST. NRO MISSION SUCCESS https://x.com/NRO_gov/status/2124514497050050808. utc shifted +476 s from the window-open T0 2026-11-22T12:16:00Z. ECEF geometry unchanged. Sim not re-run. Post-flight SpaceX timeline reads MECO 2:10, fairing 2:58, landing 7:37; the files still use the pre-flight 2:11 / 2:59 / 7:34 marks (1 s, 1 s, and 3 s). Knots were not moved. Payload is classified: no satellite count, no Starshield label, no booster serial. ILLUSTRATIVE.
RETIMED 2026-11-21 (board run ~7:50 a.m. PST): T0 is the window open 2026-11-22T12:16:00Z (Sun 22 Nov, 30-minute window opens 4:16 a.m. PT, to 12:46Z). Backup Mon 23 Nov 4:02 a.m. PT = 2026-11-23T12:02:00Z. SpaceX https://www.spacex.com/launches/nrol136 and LL2 id 951a341f-236b-42fe-a667-4ab2fcf36eac (last_updated 2026-11-20T17:43:00Z) agree on 12:16Z. utc shifted +85560 s from 2026-11-21T12:30:00Z. ECEF geometry unchanged. Sim not re-run. Published ascent events are unchanged (MECO 00:02:11, stage sep 00:02:14, SES-1 00:02:22, fairing sep 00:02:59), so the surrogate knots were not moved. First stage is the 14th flight and lands at Landing Zone 4. The earlier Saturday-versus-Sunday conflict is closed. ILLUSTRATIVE.
ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Falcon 9 NROL-136 (SLC-4E) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
PRE-FLIGHT. LL2 id 951a341f-236b-42fe-a667-4ab2fcf36eac, status Go, NET 2026-11-21T12:30:00Z (Sat 21 Nov 4:30 a.m. PST), window 12:30-13:00Z.
SpaceX nrol136 page: &#x27;targeting Saturday, November 21&#x27; from SLC-4E; 30-minute window opens at 4:30 a.m. PT; backup Sunday, November 22 at 4:16 a.m. PT. Booster 14th flight, landing LZ-4.
Loft: FALCON 9 FAMILY SURROGATE, not this flight: altitude and downrange vs time from SpaceX webcast telemetry of Iridium NEXT-7 (F9 Block 5, VSFB SLC-4E, 25 Jul 2018), the same loft rows as USSF-317 / USSF-627.
  Telemetry source: https://github.com/shahar603/Telemetry-Data/tree/master/Iridium%20NEXT%207. FILE ENDS AT T+508 s (telemetry end): NROL-136 SECO, orbit and deploy are NOT published.
Events (SpaceX nrol136 timeline https://www.spacex.com/launches/nrol136, checked 2026-11-18): Max-Q 1:02, MECO 2:11, sep 2:14, SES-1 2:22, fairing 2:59, boostback 2:27-3:22, entry 5:53-6:10, landing 7:34 on LZ-4.
Azimuth basis: USCG Local Notice to Mariners 58668 Hazard Area A far-edge midpoint. Vertices 30.9500N 118.6833W and 31.0167N 118.6167W; midpoint 30.9833N 118.6500W; bearing from the LL2 pad 155.15 deg (445 km).
  Primary time on that notice: 21 Nov 1230-1325Z. https://space-notices.com/notice/lnm-58668
  Hazard Area B of the same notice and NOTAM MMFR B4576/26 (stage 1, 21 Nov 1230-1343Z) are further downrange and were not used for the azimuth. https://www.notamify.com/notams/MMFR/b88795c4-a1ff-4e2f-a802-fc51a2519d6d
  Non-rotating inclination from 155.15 deg at this pad is 69.77 deg, which sits on the 69.7 deg of prior NRO proliferated batches. The azimuth was taken from the hazard area and was not tuned to that inclination.
ASSUMPTION: orbit and everything after the telemetry loft are borrowed from prior proliferated-architecture flights (NROL-146 and later: ~69.7 deg, Wikipedia table 425 x 310 km; Langbroek launch-night ~310 km). Not NROL-136 elements. No prior NROL trajectory file exists in this repo.
Velocity = d/dt of the family altitude and ground range (Earth-relative), laid on this azimuth.
Pad (LL2): 34.632000N -120.611000E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s.
Constant-azimuth rhumb Az=155.15 deg from pad. Velocity ECEF: v_horiz along Az + hdot Up in local ENU.
T0 used: 2026-11-22T12:23:56Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.</description>
